From eb1fe8f2e4ab7bfe7f1954f4e957c4b842cf08ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:14:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add accounts, profiles and settings, and redesign the UI

Accounts
- Register, sign in/out, forgot and reset password (single-use, 1-hour,
  hashed token; identical response whether or not the email exists)
- Session in an httpOnly SameSite=Lax cookie; tokenVersion signs out other
  devices on password change/reset; auth routes rate limited
- Public profiles at /u/:username; settings for name, username, bio, email
  (needs current password), password, and account deletion
- Anonymous device-id users are kept; registering from the same device
  claims their old visits and reviews

Access rules
- Guests can browse the map, open cafes and read logs
- Visiting, rating and the log page require sign-in, enforced on the server
- Cafe rows are only created by signed-in users and never overwritten from
  client input, so browsing no longer writes to the database

Design
- New look: ceramic ground, one variable typeface (Bricolage Grotesque),
  cherry actions, leaf-green visited state, coffee-bean ratings
- Floating dock with sliding indicator, spring bottom sheet with swipe to
  dismiss, bean roll-in and stamp-press on user actions, steaming cup on
  account screens; all motion respects prefers-reduced-motion

Also: SPA fallback rewrite in vercel.json so emailed reset links open on a
cold load; migration 20261030090000_accounts; README and .env.example updated.

